\item{\code{"error_among_accepted"}}{\code{n} is the number of items acted on at
\code{t} (those with \code{p >= t}) and \code{k} the number of those that were wrong.
For actions such as stopping, skipping or accepting.}
\item{\code{"miss_rate"}}{\code{n} is the number of items on which acting is wrong
(for screening, the eligible records) and \code{k} the number of those acted
